WEBVTT

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.050
How about earning money
as a pro baseball player?

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.100
If you use magic
to pitch at 625 miles per hour,

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.890
you can win a huge contract.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.560
Over 100 million yens guaranteed.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.320
When I was in high school, I didn't like
the guys on the baseball team.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:32.440
They acted like they owned the classroom.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.530
If so--

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:37.990
But I knew that they practiced hard,
sweating under the brutal sun.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.000
I don't want to trample on their efforts
by cheating with magic.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.750
Uncle.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.710
For about six years,
from sixth to 11th grade,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.010
I dedicated my life to Alien Soldier.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:57.390
I understand how they must've felt,
'cause I sweat like they did.

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:00.260
No way. Apologize to all the kids
who are serious about baseball.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.390
My uncle means every word.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.270
UNCLE:
YOU'RE FINE THE WAY YOU ARE

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:21.180
GET HOME

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:27.430
SOLD CHEAPER THAN A SCOURING PAD

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.650
JUNE, 2018

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:42.660
Compared to other sports,
baseball terminology sounds dangerous.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.030
You mean, dead balls and stolen bases?

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.950
And sacrifice flies and grand slams.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.040
Exactly.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:52.210
That reminds me,
I almost got assassinated once.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.290
-What?
-What?

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.750
You are dropping a bomb.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.920
Icuras elran.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.890
On this day, I was totally exhausted
from delving into a dungeon.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.230
Wait, this person…

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.110
was there when you broke
the barrier of Luvaldram.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.490
She was also there when he was with Elf.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.620
You're right. She was there.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.500
Was she waiting for the right moment?

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.620
Seriously?

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.050
Found you.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:09.700
Mabel.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.710
What's the matter?

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.170
Because you slew
the legendary blaze dragon

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:25.180
without sealing it
with the god-freezing sword,

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:30.560
you released me from my duty
to hand the sword down to an heir.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.180
Hooray!

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:35.190
Good for you. I'm glad
that my fight meant something to you.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.940
He didn't get the sarcasm at all.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:43.990
Because of my uncle,
Mabel's life spiraled.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:50.120
Why don't you draw a sword?

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:54.290
I've been plagued by the intention
to kill with Psikyo bullets,

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:55.830
so I can tell.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:00.750
You don't mean to kill me at all.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:07.720
Actually, you don't look good.
Are you eating well?

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:32.160
I know that you saved the village.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:45.420
So Mabel tried to kill me,

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.630
but, for the time being,
I took her to an inn.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.010
You dragged her.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:05:59.850
Where am I?

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.650
An inn. Here.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:08.910
What happened? I thought you wanted
to be a hermit back at home.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:16.250
When I returned, my house
had been cut down as logs for fireplaces.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.750
The mayor said
I need to provide for myself.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.210
MABEL - MANU

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:26.090
If I didn't agree to it,
he would make me a village pet.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:28.090
Another World is so messed up.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.340
That's the villagers' long-held grudges
against the Ice clan.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.140
So, which one did you choose?

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:41.060
I froze the villagers' feet
with the god-freezing sword,

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.560
dribbled some water around their necks,
then ran away.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.730
Wow, all of them?

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:47.190
All 108 villagers.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.610
Oh, my God! So tenacious.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.570
I can't go back anymore.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:54.780
You really despise working, don't you?

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.120
Well…

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.620
Surrounded by flowers in a flower shop,

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:03.920
tasting samples at a bakery,

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:07.260
cuddling fluffy stuffed animals
in a doll shop.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:12.140
I can't stand such harsh, heavy labor.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:14.300
Which part of these jobs was harsh?

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:16.350
Your standard is so damn low.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:18.470
I understand.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:22.350
Working your life away
on the daily grind in an office,

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:25.690
attending drinking parties with coworkers
when work is done,

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.570
I wouldn't be able to handle that either.

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:30.860
What? Uncle was planning on getting
a typical white-collar job?

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:33.820
Japanese society still had some leeway
18 years ago.

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:35.320
LIFE WAS ROUGH BACK THEN TOO

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:39.830
But I'm supporting myself
as an adventurer now.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:44.040
It's the best job for finding a way
back to my world.

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:46.250
That's amazing.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:48.840
I wish I could have something like that.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.340
What? "Amazing"?

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:53.470
Well, in my own world,
I did beat Alien Soldier on Superhard

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.720
in under 30 minutes.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.760
Is that supposed to be amazing?

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:59.470
Yeah, I'm an adventurer now,

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.690
thanks to the skills I learned
from video games.

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:07.900
-Your world?
-Mabel, you were a guardian all your life.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.650
Maybe you can make a living
using the god-freezing sword.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.160
The freezing magic you used earlier
was impressive.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:19.240
I, the guardian, should use
the god-freezing sword?

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.330
-But my clan kept it for 400 years.
-Like I told you before,

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:26.750
no matter what anyone says,
this is your life, Mabel.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:30.050
You choose what you want to do.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:35.930
-The power to carry through is strength.
-The power to carry through is strength.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.390
You remember it.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:47.690
For now, maybe I should find a way
to break the seal of ice completely.

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:51.610
Oh, I went to Mount Marchid
to pick powa-powa blossoms after that,

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:53.190
but nothing happened.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.280
Really?

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:58.910
The seal of ice linked up with my heart.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:03.750
Maybe, if I become an adventurer
and fix my gloomy personality,

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:05.500
I may be able to make a living.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:06.790
Gloomy?

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:09.840
I think being an introvert
is perfectly fine.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:13.510
It's not fine.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:16.970
The villagers said
my gloominess makes them depressed.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.050
My eyes look puffy too.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:20.760
I disagree.

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.220
It's fun talking with you.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:25.730
Your eyes are attractive
like Heather from Dynamite Headdy.

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:28.270
Are you sure? You are making me blush.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:32.400
Oh, that's right.
The one on your left hand.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:33.480
What?

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.740
It's worth enough to get by
for the rest of your life.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:40.910
This is to provide for your livelihood.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:41.990
Please accept it.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:44.620
No worries for the rest of my life?

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.120
What is this geezer doing?

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:49.330
This is his second time.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.840
I put it on while you were sleeping.

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:55.010
Well, but…

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:58.680
I'm sorry.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:02.760
I respect you, but it's nothing romantic.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.980
I cannot accept this.

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.480
It's melting!

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.690
Her icy heart, gone in a second.

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:12.730
Yes, yes. It's okay, really.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:15.650
No, it's not good.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:19.700
Why? I rejected him, right? I did.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:22.160
I said no, right?

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:25.290
I found it while exploring today.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.080
Maybe this was meant to be.

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:33.040
There are only seven cosmite rings
in the world, and this is one of them.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.500
This is my token of apology.

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:36.760
I can't accept such a precious ring.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:39.510
Well, it's late now.
Stay here for tonight.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:43.220
It's a small bed,
so there's not much room for two.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.680
As Elf is staying here too,
she may let you stay in her room.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:48.770
-Excuse me.
-What?

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.440
Do you have change I can use
for the public bath?

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:55.110
I haven't bathed in a while.

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:56.360
Do you think you stink?

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:02.990
You smell a little earthy,
but it's not a bad smell.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:06.200
Don't smell me!

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:11.080
Well, if you sell the ring,
you can afford the bathing fee.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:13.750
What? Sell the ring?

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:15.340
Yes.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:19.420
As I said, sell the ring and never worry
about money for the rest of your life.

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:37.820
Hey, orc face! It's late in the night.

00:11:38.570 --> 00:11:41.530
Did the orc instinct
turn you into a pervert?

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:44.410
If you don't mind, I can sleep with you.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:11.100
He turned me down.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:15.060
Hey, you. Lend me a hand.
She is out of control.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:23.950
I see.

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:28.530
What are you doing? Stop it.

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:32.040
My defense is low because I spent
my spirits in the dungeon earlier today.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:54.270
And that's how I was almost assassinated

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:56.940
and sealed with ice
until the next morning.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:58.150
Isn't that horrible?

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:00.400
-Yeah.
-Yes.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:03.360
-You were horrible.
-You were horrible.

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.320
Still, you are amazing.

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:09.280
You said you beat Alien Soldier
in 30 minutes?

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:13.120
To be precise,
it was 29 minutes and 29 seconds.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.000
I was so into it.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:16.500
Really?

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:21.960
I intentionally didn't use Homing Force.
But that was the key.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:24.760
Just run through with Ranger Force
for easy battles…

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:27.340
I found a video online.
Someone beat it in 12 minutes.

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:37.850
How dare you, Internet?

00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:40.310
It's not the Internet's fault, Uncle.

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:45.190
Speaking of the Internet,

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:50.120
what does it mean
by the North American version of the game?

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.620
Oh, you mean the region-coded games.

00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:56.710
The same game can be in
different languages by the sales regions.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:59.120
If it's in English, I'd be in trouble.

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:02.590
But I kind of understand what's said
at the beginning of Altered Beast.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:06.300
Like, "Go, brave men, to defeat the evil."

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:08.380
Wait, let me use a translation app.

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:14.850
Rise from your grave.

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:15.930
Grave?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:18.100
Was the main character a dead man?

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:20.560
You were totally off.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:22.060
Why is that?

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:23.650
Maybe the blood of Another World.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.030
Wait, they are still talking.

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:29.990
Maybe he shares our blood,
the blood of the Ice clan.

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:34.450
Because he is a transferee
from Irellars Japan Bahamal.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:37.290
Wait, she just said…

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:39.920
ALL CREATION - RESIDENCE
ICE STORM

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:43.290
-Hey, she just said "Japan Bahamal."
-What?

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:44.880
How do they know about Japan?

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.010
Let's take a look.

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:51.300
What a disaster that he put the ring
on you while you were sleeping.

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:53.350
Marriage while sleeping,

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.810
rather, a forced marriage by an orc
while sleeping,

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.560
it's a lifelong trauma.

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:02.270
No one would marry you
after you married a filthy orc.

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:03.770
Don't despair.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:11.950
Actually, you don't seem to mind it.
Why is that?

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:16.950
Maybe the blood of Another World.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:22.250
Maybe he shares our blood,
the blood of the Ice clan.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:25.840
Because he is a transferee
from Irellars Japan Bahamal.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:31.550
I see.
They talked while I was sealed in ice.

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:34.350
They were talking about Japan, right?

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:40.060
Raybelio yuul elran.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:48.280
The patriarch of the Ice clan

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:53.200
was a knight from Japan Bahamal
about 400 years ago.

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:57.790
He lost his life in a war
in Japan Bahamal.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:16:02.250
He was given a new body and life
in Granbahamal.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:05.460
Then he received a message from God.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:07.670
"Hear me, transferee.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:12.380
I shall grant you one wish
to survive this harsh world."

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:15.640
The knight responded with his wish.

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:18.890
"Give me a sword that can slay you."

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:23.100
Divine bonus, a classic pattern
of the Isekai reincarnation fantasy.

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:25.100
The samurai's reply was rebellious
and so cool.

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:26.230
What did the god say?

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:28.980
The god responded,

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:31.780
"You wish to have the power to slay God.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.990
Ha ha, how interesting."

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:38.450
Moreover, does that ugly orc face
look like a human to you?

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:41.000
-"Ha ha, how interesting."
-Is it because you share a homeland?

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.290
-"Interesting."
-Seriously?

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:43.660
-"Interesting."
-You can't mean that.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:48.540
It's getting interesting.

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:51.420
-Could you be a little patient?
-I read a book about hometowns.

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:52.800
Shoo, shoo.

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:57.340
The knight acquired the god-freezing sword
and studied at the Shrine of Wisdom,

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:59.890
fell in love with a shrine maiden,
broke the seal of the sword,

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:01.560
and slew the legendary blaze dragon.

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:03.890
It's been kept in the clan
for generations.

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:09.150
She just spoiled the best part!

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:13.860
Back to my point,
do you see the orc face as…

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:18.160
Telling this story was the only thing
I'm confident at.

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:23.120
All my practice efforts…

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:26.370
I'm sorry. Don't cry.

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.130
There, there.

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:32.880
I didn't get that.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:33.960
-Huh?
-What?

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:37.590
I didn't get such a great bonus
like the god-freezing sword!

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:42.100
You must have received magic power
as the divine bonus.

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:45.350
I didn't get any bonus!
Actually, I even didn't talk with a god!

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:49.520
Then let's look at the moment
you were transferred 18 years ago.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.610
-You're right.
-Eighteen years?

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:53.360
Can you rewind that many years?

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:55.990
It's been a long time
and may take a while to search.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:58.360
Well…

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:01.950
Mob lynches, execution, execution…

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:03.830
He's mumbling disturbing things.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:07.210
He was hunted down as an orc variant
from the very beginning.

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.290
Seriously?

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:09.370
Found it.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.550
You shitty orc!
Are you trying to eat my cow?

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:15.550
No, Uncle. This isn't the right one.

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:16.630
Then how about this one?

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:20.180
Burn this pagan evil orc!

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:22.260
It's the time you made the magical vase.

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:23.970
-This one?
-Nope.

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:25.350
-How about this one?
-Nope.

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:27.060
Then this one.

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:28.850
You've been hunted too many times!

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:31.480
I'm a real heavy sleeper.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.940
If I was attacked while asleep,
I couldn't avoid getting hanged.

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:36.400
I wonder how you survived
to tell the tale.

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:37.950
How about this?

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:40.780
What's going on?

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:43.620
It's similar to the resurrection spell
of divine magic.

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:47.080
I thought I found this magic
much later on.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.160
Why does this appear in an old memory?

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:53.170
Wait. Isn't that you when you were 17,
right when you arrived in Another World?

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.250
I see.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:58.130
This was how my body was formed
in Granbahamal.

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:04.390
Did a god create your body?

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:05.680
Seems like it.

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:13.980
This is where I was mistaken for
an orc variant and got beat up.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:17.990
I didn't know their language,
but I offered them my money.

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:21.490
They mistook the cash for spell cards
and beat me even more.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:28.540
January, 2000. I was gonna buy new video
games with my holiday money envelopes.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:32.080
I was so happy, but got in an accident
on the way, and the rest is history.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:34.670
What was I going to buy?

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:37.170
-What a heavy story.
-What a heavy story.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:41.340
Wait. I hear something.

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:43.390
Could it be the god's voice?

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:45.640
Wait, let me turn up the volume.

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:49.640
I'm the god of Another World,
and you are a transferee.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:51.690
To survive this harsh world…

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:55.860
-No idea what is being said.
-Maybe the god mixed up the region code.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:20:00.030
I couldn't hear it
while I was getting clobbered senseless.

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:03.200
Uncle, I will translate it.
Please rewind 30 seconds.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.410
Okay.

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:08.120
Hello, dear customers.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:09.200
WELCOME TO GRANBAHAMAL

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:10.370
In-store announcement?

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:12.830
Totally prerecorded.

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:17.540
She is saying, "I will give you power."
It's just as Mabel said.

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:21.590
I see. What I wished at that moment
became my ability.

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:23.340
Your powers must have awakened then.

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:26.050
You can triumph
with unrivaled magic power now.

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:29.640
Your wish was "I want the power
to exterminate these shitheads."

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:34.850
Or "Make them miserable and
make them regret ever being born." Right?

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:39.440
Takafumi, did something happen to you
while you were in high school?

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:40.610
HIS FAMILY FELL APART

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:43.900
No, what I was thinking was…

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:46.200
If only I could…

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:49.700
If only I could speak their language,
we could understand each other.

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:51.450
Oh, this one.

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:55.620
Well…

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:59.290
"Approved. Your wish has been granted.

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:04.550
You can acquire the minimum knowledge
if you go to Mount Dordo," said God.

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.800
So, then, Uncle's magic power was…

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:08.850
-translation?
-Guess so.

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:09.930
So lame.

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:14.640
Suddenly, I understood their language,
but I guess that was my bonus.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:19.650
So you could have learned the language
at Mount Dordo?

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:22.990
…am not…

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:27.410
I'm not an orc!

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:30.240
Oh, I see.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:32.790
This is how you spoke to each other.

00:21:32.870 --> 00:21:35.870
Well, this is quite expected of Uncle,
in a way.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:36.960
No.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:41.670
I was sold to a freak show as a rare orc
who understood human words.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:45.800
I cost three bronze coins.

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:49.220
-And then…
-Wait, Uncle!

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:52.600
I want a cup of coffee.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:54.640
Me too.

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:58.100
That's a good idea.
Let's have a coffee break.

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:04.070
The god seemed to have lost interest
in his responsibilities.

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:07.320
And the residents of Another World
were shitty, as always.

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:12.030
The terribly heavy story
seemed to have no end,

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:14.660
so we decided to have a coffee break.

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:17.290
-Delish.
-Good beans.

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:19.790
What a profoundly deep flavor.

00:23:46.710 --> 00:23:50.920
Subtitle translation by:
Megumi Hunter
